+\cite[\S12.7]{FresanJossenExp}.  The homogeneous polynomial-phase
+Fourier--Laplace construction is given in
+\cite[Proposition~5.1]{FresanJossen}.  Jossen's 2025 lecture, reporting joint
+work in progress with Fres\'an, treats the quadratic marked-point model and
+explains the independence of its compact integrals and endpoint
+exponentials, apart from an additional $\sqrt\pi$-direction in the full
+rapid-decay period problem \cite{Jossen2025}.  The contribution here is the
+uniform linear transfer theorem for arbitrary polynomial phases and
+amplitudes, allowing different phases in one relation, and the realization
+of every resulting relation by the stated formal period operations.  The
+simultaneous-cover argument supplies this last step; it is not a consequence
+of lifting alone.
