+independence furnished by Siegel--Shidlovskii theory \cite{Jossen2025}.
+For the compact integral $F_a(z)=\int_0^a e^{-zx^2}\,dx$, the normalization
+$F_a(z)/a$ for $a\ne0$ depends only on $a^2$; the raw integrals satisfy
+$F_{-a}=-F_a$.  The quadratic model is therefore a predecessor of the
+translation-group description below.  The present
+result gives the uniform affine-linear relation ideal for arbitrary
+polynomial phases, amplitudes, and boundary data, and identifies its
+specialized generators by formal period operations.  It does not address
+the extra $\sqrt\pi$-independence question in the full quadratic rapid-decay
+period field.
